-- GAME ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Title       Lode Runner
  Publisher   Software Projects, 1984
  Version     1.0

-- YOU NEED ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your own copy of the original game, saved beside this patch:

  File        Lode Runner (1984)(Software Projects)(128K).z80
  MD5         41360f6c33e7a02ca6450881cb385ade

  The patch carries none of the game's code. It only works with that exact
  dump, under that name or any other: anything else is refused, with a
  message naming the file it wants.

-- WHAT IT DOES --------------------------------------------------------------
  Moving figures become Next hardware sprites, so they keep their own colours
  and no longer take on the scenery's (colour clash). Game logic is unchanged.

  Pace        original (-0.00% measured in JNext 1.1.104 headless, the plain
              .nex as control, input keyed to the runner's update 0x92FC,
              lockstep checked at every update)

  Changes     1.0: Dean Woodyatt's Lode Runner engine rebuilt on the 128K
              release (AY music), with the whole alt ROM image and the start-
              up checks

  Note        The 128K release, so the AY music plays. Dean Woodyatt's engine,
              unchanged: the runner and the guards are hardware sprites in the
              game's colours, the scenery keeps its own. The alt ROM holds the
              128K machine's ROM 1, so the fade between lives looks as on a
              real 128K.

-- MENU ----------------------------------------------------------------------
   1  Infinite lives
   2  Immunity

  Cheats come from the archive's POKEs for this release.

