-- TESTING -------------------------------------------------------------------
  Tested      Played by the owner in JNext 2026-11-05: approved

  Replay      4 recordings of the 128K release IDENTICAL on Dean's engine
              (rework v2): 3 bot RZX of 20,042 / 20,021 / 20,049 frames + a
              6,000-frame free run (registers, memory, sprite pixels vs the
              plotter, the patched screen frame by frame, every screen /
              attribute read); every hook ran (draws 14,859 + 24 runner,
              erases 14,882, guard death 0x96B6 1 with its respawn draw
              0x970C, level-start prints 60 + 240, paints 42,210, fades and
              clears 96); 6,074 unit cases PASS, 3 negative controls detected;
              clock matrix 8 hook sites x 4 incoming clocks = 32 cases, exit
              speed = the incoming one, a forced 3.5 MHz exit detected; ROM
              paths: every ROM byte as recorded but the 20-byte start-up
              register block (known, read only by the fade); start-up tail
              never read before written

  Emulator    JNext 1.1.104 headless: reaches play, AY music written (146-169
              data writes a second, as the original); flicker 300 frames: 0
              out of step, 0 vanished; 15-minute soak against the original
              .z80: no freeze, loop or crash, game overs and restarts in both;
              frames viewed; no person played it

  Coverage    level 1 only (the bot dies there); a guard trapped by a
              refilling brick once; no level complete, editor, load / save
              screens or redefine keys; cheats proved in the simulator on the
              original 128K file: Infinite lives: 17 deaths, lives held at 5
              (without: 5 to 0, game over); Immunity: guard touches never kill
              (0x9CD2 death path 0 times, 15 without), deaths by a refilling
              brick still happen

  Hardware    none

  Nothing here claims a result on real hardware unless the line above says so.

-- HOW TO USE ----------------------------------------------------------------
  Put this .nxc and the game file in the same folder on the Next's card and
  choose the .nxc in the Browser. See README.txt.
